WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.962
The former president indicted.

00:00:03.962 --> 00:00:05.547
That is according to Have

00:00:05.547 --> 00:00:06.381
and other sources

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:08.258
confirming it to CNN tonight.

00:00:08.258 --> 00:00:08.800
Joining us

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.177
now is one of his attorneys, Jim Trusty.

00:00:11.386 --> 00:00:12.554
This is his first interview

00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:14.681
since news of the indictment broke

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:15.890
just a few hours ago.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.559
Jim, thanks for joining us.

00:00:17.559 --> 00:00:18.351
My first question,

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:20.603
do you have a copy of this indictment?

00:00:22.772 --> 00:00:23.982
No, we haven't been provided

00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:24.983
with the indictment yet.

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:25.900
What we have right now

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.485
is essentially a summons,

00:00:27.485 --> 00:00:29.571
which is a replacement for a warrant.

00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:29.904
Right.

00:00:29.904 --> 00:00:30.905
Normally, indictments

00:00:30.905 --> 00:00:32.198
are accompanied by a warrant

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.324
where there's an arrest.

00:00:33.324 --> 00:00:35.326
Here, we've received a summons

00:00:35.326 --> 00:00:36.786
from the Department of Justice

00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:38.079
asking us to be

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:40.665
at the courthouse Tuesday at 3:00.

00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:41.416
And does it say

00:00:41.416 --> 00:00:42.876
how many charges there are

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:43.793
against your client?

00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:46.713
It again, it

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.590
doesn't perfectly mirror an indictment,

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.467
but it does have some language in it

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:51.134
that suggests

00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:53.303
what the seven charges would be.

00:00:53.303 --> 00:00:54.304
Not 100% clear

00:00:54.304 --> 00:00:55.764
that all of those are separate charges,

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:57.432
but they basically break out

00:00:57.432 --> 00:00:59.559
from an Espionage Act charge,

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.102
which is ludicrous

00:01:01.102 --> 00:01:02.437
under the facts of this case.

00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:04.064
And I can certainly explain it.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.648
And several obstruction

00:01:05.648 --> 00:01:07.150
based type charges

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.735
and then false statement charges,

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.361
which are actually, again,

00:01:10.361 --> 00:01:11.946
kind of a crazy stretch

00:01:11.946 --> 00:01:13.281
just from the facts as we know it.

00:01:13.281 --> 00:01:14.908
So there's a lot to pick out

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.201
eventually from the defense side,

00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:18.036
but that appears to be the charges.

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:19.329
And it appears to be something

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:21.664
that will get off the ground on Tuesday.

00:01:21.664 --> 00:01:21.998
Okay.

00:01:21.998 --> 00:01:22.749
So you're confirming

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.042
it is seven charges

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:25.585
You said there's an Espionage

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.378
Espionage Act charge.

00:01:27.378 --> 00:01:28.713
Is there one on the willful

00:01:28.713 --> 00:01:30.006
retention of documents

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.009
Yeah, that's it.

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:34.177
We're talking to 18 U.S.C.

00:01:34.177 --> 00:01:35.970
seven 93

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:37.597
and then there are several 18 U.S.C.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.474
15, 12, 15, 19.

00:01:39.474 --> 00:01:39.808
It's great

00:01:39.808 --> 00:01:40.517
television, right,

00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:41.726
to cite these numbers

00:01:41.726 --> 00:01:42.644
but the bottom line is it

00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:44.437
breaks down to the retention charge,

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:45.438
as you would call it,

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.732
obstructions and false statement.

00:01:47.732 --> 00:01:49.901
And is there a conspiracy charge in here?

00:01:51.986 --> 00:01:52.987
I believe so.

00:01:52.987 --> 00:01:54.405
I don't have in front of me right now.

00:01:54.405 --> 00:01:54.739
Again,

00:01:54.739 --> 00:01:55.865
this is not

00:01:55.865 --> 00:01:57.075
biblically accurate

00:01:57.075 --> 00:01:57.951
because I'm not looking

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:58.993
at a charging document.

00:01:58.993 --> 00:02:00.328
I'm looking at a summary sheet.

00:02:00.328 --> 00:02:01.871
So there's language in there

00:02:01.871 --> 00:02:03.498
that might actually be

00:02:03.498 --> 00:02:05.416
reflecting a single count instead of two,

00:02:05.416 --> 00:02:06.042
but I think there was

00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:07.836
a conspiracy count as well.

00:02:07.836 --> 00:02:09.879
And so that means there could be

00:02:09.879 --> 00:02:11.548
other indictments Have you told that

00:02:11.548 --> 00:02:12.590
have you been told that anyone else

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:13.424
was indicted here?

00:02:15.677 --> 00:02:16.177
We weren't

00:02:16.177 --> 00:02:18.388
advised of anyone else being indicted.

00:02:19.347 --> 00:02:20.181
I have a theory

00:02:20.181 --> 00:02:20.807
that maybe

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:23.017
some of the outrageous misconduct

00:02:23.268 --> 00:02:24.686
has affected the equation.

00:02:24.686 --> 00:02:27.188
In some other case, a potential target.

00:02:27.188 --> 00:02:28.815
But bottom line is, right now,

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.942
all we know about is our client.

00:02:30.942 --> 00:02:33.153
What's your theory?

00:02:34.362 --> 00:02:36.322
Well, over the last 24 hours,

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.740
it's become public

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:38.908
that members

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:39.492
of the Department

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.202
of Justice, led by Jay Brad,

00:02:41.202 --> 00:02:42.370
who is a pivotal figure

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:43.371
in this investigation,

00:02:43.371 --> 00:02:45.248
This is the guy who wanted to do a raid

00:02:45.248 --> 00:02:47.542
before they even had a subpoena out.

00:02:47.542 --> 00:02:48.293
He apparently,

00:02:48.293 --> 00:02:48.710
along with

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:49.711
five other people

00:02:49.711 --> 00:02:52.589
in his presence from DOJ, extorted

00:02:52.922 --> 00:02:54.257
a very well-respected,

00:02:54.257 --> 00:02:55.466
very intelligent lawyer

00:02:55.466 --> 00:02:57.051
from Washington, D.C.,

00:02:57.051 --> 00:02:58.136
saying essentially,

00:02:58.136 --> 00:02:59.596
if you want this judgeship

00:02:59.596 --> 00:03:01.848
that's on Joe Biden's desk,

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:04.267
you have to flip your guy to cooperate

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:05.643
against the president

00:03:05.643 --> 00:03:06.436
of the United States.

00:03:06.436 --> 00:03:08.229
That's the headline evidence.

00:03:08.229 --> 00:03:08.730
I know that

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.899
that's that's been something that

00:03:10.899 --> 00:03:12.066
Republican allies of Trump

00:03:12.066 --> 00:03:12.525
have been saying.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:13.735
But do you have evidence

00:03:13.735 --> 00:03:15.278
that that happened?

00:03:15.278 --> 00:03:16.571
Yeah, this is

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.698
this is no political talker.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.116
This is something that was reported

00:03:20.116 --> 00:03:21.910
at the time by the attorney.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.913
It has been basically sworn to by him.

00:03:24.913 --> 00:03:25.747
He's written a letter

00:03:25.747 --> 00:03:27.582
that's been submitted to a U.S.

00:03:27.582 --> 00:03:28.499
